NULL)`, and compares byte-for-byte. Randomized rows use fixed-seed xorshift64\\*.\n\nCoverage highlights: all 5 entry points including the low-level ones; full non-NUL byte domain and exhaustive `0x01..=0xFF` sweep; invalid UTF-8; `printf` format-specifier payloads (`%n`, `%1000000d`) as data; embedded NULs; stdio-buffer-boundary lengths (1023…65537) and a 1 MiB payload; `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX`/decimal-width boundaries/4096 random `i32`; a 64-bit-wide argument passed to the `int` prototype; and randomized interleavings of all 5 entry points sharing one `stdout` buffer.\n\n**Result: 352 checks, 0 failures**, in debug and release.\n\n## Harness validated by negative controls\n\nPassing tests only mean something if the harness can fail, so I injected two bugs into `src/lib.rs`, confirmed detection, then restored (diff-verified identical, `grep -c NEGATIVE_CONTROL` = 0):\n\n- `good()` summing to 3 → **73 failures** (`cfg_17`, `cfg_19`, `cfg_20`, `cfg_21`, `err_13`)\n- `printLine(NULL)` printing a newline → **55 failures** (`cfg_01`, `err_01`, `err_01_interleaved`)\n\nNo divergences were found, so `src/lib.rs` needed no fixes; the only source changes were `Cargo.toml` (`libloading` dev-dep + test target), the three artifacts, `tests/differential.rs`, and `verify.sh`. Nothing in `c_src/` was modified — only the `build/` directory was added."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":598,"cache_read_input_tokens":82301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":598,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7d292cdd-55d8-4270-aa1d-136cdbbefa1e","uuid":"fff99d1e-125b-4c78-95fb-bac357aabecd","timestamp":"2026-08-18T02:06:07.921Z"}
